    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane containing the three points
(2, -3, 5), (6, -2, 4), (6, -1, 6) in which the coefficient of <m>x</m> is 3.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\mathopen{}\left(x-2\right)+\left(-8\right)\mathopen{}\left(y-\left(-3\right)\right)+4\mathopen{}\left(z-5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
